    <briefdescription>
<para>Current <computeroutput><ref refid="class_ints_set" kindref="compound">IntsSet</ref></computeroutput> configuration: exposes <computeroutput><ref refid="class_module_monom_default_config_a80ac394f6cdf74921227ead9bdd730b3_1a80ac394f6cdf74921227ead9bdd730b3" kindref="member">Hash</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="class_module_monom_default_config_ab1710698369de78731b7e526d379ba74_1ab1710698369de78731b7e526d379ba74" kindref="member">Eq</ref></computeroutput> as discrete member functors so the <computeroutput>unordered_set</computeroutput> can use them directly. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Used by the type alias <computeroutput><ref refid="monomial-collection_8hpp_a3ff66fa0172547637ea18786761e8241_1a3ff66fa0172547637ea18786761e8241" kindref="member">ModuleMonomialSet</ref> = <ref refid="class_ints_set" kindref="compound">IntsSet</ref>&lt;<ref refid="class_module_monom_default_config" kindref="compound">ModuleMonomDefaultConfig</ref>&gt;</computeroutput>. The constructor takes the variable count for size accounting; the old single-functor <computeroutput>hash</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>keysEqual</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>display</computeroutput> interface is kept under <computeroutput>#if 0</computeroutput> for reference until the refactor lands. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
